      "writtenOn": "2020-09-17T04:18:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In terms of host command structure, I was thinking we\u0027ll try to future-plan by reserving ourselves a good sized data section that the sub-commands can use.  The contents of the data section would be interpreted based on the sub-command and we should hopefully be able to get away without having to version the host command much as we add new sub-commands (versioning would probably be necessary if we end up changing one of the sub-command\u0027s data structures though, I\u0027d imagine).  \n\nWhat do you think?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 6361,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 6364,
        "endChar": 14
      },
      "revId": "5617cb7d11d055087ff8a1281cb9628c0de4f8e3",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
